          "python",
          "import torch.optim as optim\n\n# Weight decay in optimizer\noptimizer = optim.Adam(model.parameters(), lr=0.001, weight_decay=0.0001)\n\n# weight_decay=0 (default) \u2192 no regularization\n# weight_decay=0.0001 \u2192 typical value\n# weight_decay=0.01 \u2192 strong regularization\n\n# Practical: adjust based on validation performance\n# If overfitting: increase weight_decay\n# If underfitting: decrease weight_decay"
